-- title:
--   Compact open subsets are closed in the constructible topology
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a topological space. Its *constructible topology* is the topology generated by the compact open subsets of $X$ and their complements.
--
--   **Lemma.** If $s \subseteq X$ is compact and open, then $s$ is closed in the constructible topology of $X$.
--
--   Together with the evident openness of such sets, this shows that compact opens are clopen in the constructible topology. That is a basic step in studying spectral spaces through their constructible (patch) topology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The lemma is `IsCompact.isClosed_constructibleTopology_of_isOpen`, with conclusion `IsClosed[constructibleTopology X] s`. No spectral hypothesis on $X$ is needed. The proof shows that the complement $X \setminus s$ belongs to the generating subbasis `constructibleTopologySubbasis`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/Topology/Spectral/ConstructibleTopology.lean (declarations needed by the transplanted proofs, unused ones removed).

import Mathlib.Topology.Spectral.ConstructibleTopology

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.defeqAttrib.useBackward true
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
open Topology

variable {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- A compact open is closed in the constructible topology. -/
lemma IsCompact.isClosed_constructibleTopology_of_isOpen {s : Set X}
    (hs : IsCompact s) (ho : IsOpen s) : IsClosed[constructibleTopology X] s := by
  rw [← @isOpen_compl_iff]
  apply TopologicalSpace.isOpen_generateFrom_of_mem
  simp [constructibleTopologySubbasis, ho, hs]


